-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"status\":\"generating\",\"createdBy\":\"f5dfb377-dac7-46a6-aea3-a4e04cb45e54\",\"metadata\":{\"brief\":\"Using the Feature-Benefit (FAB) framework, this top-of-funnel discovery ad targets skincare optimizers looking to upgrade their basic moisturizers to high-performance formulas without irritation. The visual hero is the product's advanced formula, depicted through a premium, minimalist studio composition where the frosted pale-blue SNIQUE Bakuchi Matte jar rests on a block of raw, textured stone, surrounded by clean splashes of water and delicate green cica leaves. The background is a clean, solid Pure White, reflecting a premium editorial aesthetic. The short, high-contrast headline in All-Caps Jost Bold reads \\\"DITCH RETINOL. TRY GENTLE BAKUCHIOL.\\\" in Slate Navy, taking up less than 10% of the space. The single call to action is a soft \\\"See how it works\\\" pill-shaped badge in Electric Blue at the bottom. To keep the ad on-brand, employ sharp-edged design elements, crisp typography with generous spacing, a high-contrast layout, and clean, high-resolution product photography that makes the pale-blue and white packaging pop against the monochromatic setting.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the Feature-Benefit (FAB) framework, this top-of-funnel discovery ad targets skincare optimizers looking to 