 high-performance formulas without irritation. The visual hero is the product's advanced formula, depicted through a premium, minimalist studio composition where the frosted pale-blue SNIQUE Bakuchi Matte jar rests on a block of raw, textured stone, surrounded by clean splashes of water and delicate green cica leaves. The background is a clean, solid Pure White, reflecting a premium editorial aesthetic. The short, high-contrast headline in All-Caps Jost Bold reads \\\"DITCH RETINOL. TRY GENTLE BAKUCHIOL.\\\" in Slate Navy, taking up less than 10% of the space. The single call to action is a soft \\\"See how it works\\\" pill-shaped badge in Electric Blue at the bottom. To keep the ad on-brand, employ sharp-edged design elements, crisp typography with generous spacing, a high-contrast layout, and clean, high-resolution product photography that makes the pale-blue and white packaging pop against the monochromatic setting.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This skin care product set consists of a 50-gram moisturizer in a cylindrical jar and its corresponding square paperboard carton. The jar features a thick-walled, frosted, semi-translucent pale-blue body—likely made of glass or heavy plastic—topped with a flush-fitting, opaque, matte white cylindrical screw cap. A white adhesive label on the front of the jar displays the text \\\"Bakuchi Matte\\\" over \\\"Hydrator Moisturizer\\\" in a bold, dark gray sans-serif font, underlined by a thin light-blue line, with a left-aligned list of six product benefits and \\\"NET QTY.: 50 gm\\\" at the bottom right. The brand name \\\"sniQue\\\" is printed vertically along the label's right edge in a light-blue stylized typeface. The matching matte-finish outer carton is primarily white with a contrasting solid light-blue band wrapping around the bottom fifth of the box. The front of the carton replicates the jar's typography and vertical brand logo, but adds a horizontal, rounded light-blue capsule printed with \\\"Ceramides + Hyaluronic Acid + Bakuchiol\\\" positioned within the bottom band. The carton's side panels present lists of ingredients, directions, and warnings in dark gray text under light-blue headers, maintaining the clean, two-tone layout.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nThe final attached image is the official brand logo. Add it once, subtly, in clean negative space; keep it exact, legible, and uncropped.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"status\":\"generating\",\"createdBy\":\"f5dfb377-dac7-46a6-aea3-a4e04cb45e54\",\"metadata\":{\"brief\":\"Using the Feature-Benefit (FAB) framework, this top-of-funnel discovery ad targets skincare optimizers looking to upgrade their basic moisturizers to high-performance formulas without irritation. The visual hero is the product's advanced formula, depicted through a premium, minimalist studio composition where the frosted pale-blue SNIQUE Bakuchi Matte jar rests on a block of raw, textured stone, surrounded by clean splashes of water and delicate green cica leaves. The background is a clean, solid Pure White, reflecting a premium editorial aesthetic. The short, high-contrast headline in All-Caps Jost Bold reads \\\"DITCH RETINOL. TRY GENTLE BAKUCHIOL.\\\" in Slate Navy, taking up less than 10% of the space. The single call to action is a soft \\\"See how it works\\\" pill-shaped badge in Electric Blue at the bottom. To keep the ad on-brand, employ sharp-edged design elements, crisp typography with generous spacing, a high-contrast layout, and clean, high-resolution product photography that makes the pale-blue and white packaging pop against the monochromatic setting.\",\"prompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the Feature-Benefit (FAB) framework, this top-of-funnel discovery ad targets skincare optimizers looking to upgrade their basic moisturizers to high-performance formulas without irritation. The visual hero is the product's advanced formula, depicted through a premium, minimalist studio composition where the frosted pale-blue SNIQUE Bakuchi Matte jar rests on a block of raw, textured stone, surrounded by clean splashes of water and delicate green cica leaves. The background is a clean, solid Pure White, reflecting a premium editorial aesthetic. The short, high-contrast headline in All-Caps Jost Bold reads \\\"DITCH RETINOL. TRY GENTLE BAKUCHIOL.\\\" in Slate Navy, taking up less than 10% of the space. The single call to action is a soft \\\"See how it works\\\" pill-shaped badge in Electric Blue at the bottom. To keep the ad on-brand, employ sharp-edged design elements, crisp typography with generous spacing, a high-contrast layout, and clean, high-resolution product photography that makes the pale-blue and white packaging pop against the monochromatic setting.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This skin care product set consists of a 50-gram moisturizer in a cylindrical jar and its corresponding square paperboard carton. The jar features a thick-walled, frosted, semi-translucent pale-blue body—likely made of glass or heavy plastic—topped with a flush-fitting, opaque, matte white cylindrical screw cap. A white adhesive label on the front of the jar displays the text \\\"Bakuchi Matte\\\" over \\\"Hydrator Moisturizer\\\" in a bold, dark gray sans-serif font, underlined by a thin light-blue line, with a left-aligned list of six product benefits and \\\"NET QTY.: 50 gm\\\" at the bottom right. The brand name \\\"sniQue\\\" is printed vertically along the label's right edge in a light-blue stylized typeface. The matching matte-finish outer carton is primarily white with a contrasting solid light-blue band wrapping around the bottom fifth of the box. The front of the carton replicates the jar's typography and vertical brand logo, but adds a horizontal, rounded light-blue capsule printed with \\\"Ceramides + Hyaluronic Acid + Bakuchiol\\\" positioned within the bottom band. The carton's side panels present lists of ingredients, directions, and warnings in dark gray text under light-blue headers, maintaining the clean, two-tone layout.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nThe final attached image is the official brand logo. Add it once, subtly, in clean negative space; keep it exact, legibl